1
00:02:15,880 --> 00:02:17,010
Here we are.

2
00:02:25,470 --> 00:02:26,610
Ready?

3
00:02:32,570 --> 00:02:34,410
"The Rains of Castamere."

4
00:02:34,440 --> 00:02:36,120
You fucking deaf?

5
00:02:36,310 --> 00:02:38,790
Same wrong guess every fucking time.

6
00:02:38,830 --> 00:02:40,080
Listen, you cunt.

7
00:02:45,320 --> 00:02:47,460
"The Bear and the Maiden Fair."

8
00:02:49,230 --> 00:02:50,770
There's a man with an ear.

9
00:02:50,950 --> 00:02:53,600
Too bad you got a hangnail for a cock.

10
00:02:55,550 --> 00:02:57,610
First time I saw you with your breeches down,

11
00:02:57,610 --> 00:02:59,180
I thought you were a eunuch.

12
00:03:00,290 --> 00:03:01,770
You've seen it, girls.

13
00:03:01,770 --> 00:03:04,620
Like a baby snail peeking out of his shell.

14
00:03:19,070 --> 00:03:21,030
Your baby was crying this morning.

15
00:03:26,750 --> 00:03:27,930
Woke me up.

16
00:03:29,630 --> 00:03:30,670
You hear me?

17
00:03:30,830 --> 00:03:32,190
Yes.

18
00:03:32,390 --> 00:03:34,920
Well, got anything to say?

19
00:03:34,930 --> 00:03:37,090
I'm sorry he woke you up.

20
00:03:38,000 --> 00:03:40,020
I don't care if you're sorry.

21
00:03:40,860 --> 00:03:42,690
Keep that baby quiet

22
00:03:42,960 --> 00:03:44,150
or I will.

23
00:03:44,460 --> 00:03:46,120
Don't you ever touch him.

24
00:03:48,070 --> 00:03:50,460
Little wildling bitch.

25
00:03:51,240 --> 00:03:53,650
You should have stayed with your own kind.

26
00:03:55,980 --> 00:03:57,290
You listening to me?

27
00:03:57,290 --> 00:03:59,510
-Shut your mouth.  -What?

28
00:04:02,320 --> 00:04:04,240
It's just an owl, you dumb bitch.

29
00:04:04,270 --> 00:04:05,870
No, it's not.

30
00:05:54,560 --> 00:05:56,530
I should never have left her there.

31
00:05:56,970 --> 00:06:00,070
-You couldn't have known.  -Of course, I could've known.

32
00:06:00,660 --> 00:06:02,730
They've been raiding the villages close by.

33
00:06:02,730 --> 00:06:05,090
And we just cower in here, while they slaughter our brothers.

34
00:06:05,090 --> 00:06:07,170
Our brothers had orders to stay at Castle Black.

35
00:06:07,170 --> 00:06:08,180
So it's all right, then?

36
00:06:08,180 --> 00:06:10,700
Black Jack and Kegs and Mully chopped to pieces,

37
00:06:10,700 --> 00:06:11,920
'cause they broke the rules?

38
00:06:11,920 --> 00:06:13,290
I didn't say it was all right.

39
00:06:13,290 --> 00:06:14,770
I'm saying they shouldn't have been there.

40
00:06:14,780 --> 00:06:17,330
We're pledged to guard the realms of men.

41
00:06:17,340 --> 00:06:18,600
She's dead because of me.

42
00:06:18,600 --> 00:06:20,120
We can't even guard Mole's Town.

43
00:06:20,120 --> 00:06:21,960
We can't go after them. You know that.

44
00:06:22,500 --> 00:06:23,900
It's what they want.

45
00:06:24,580 --> 00:06:26,050
And little Sam.

46
00:06:26,550 --> 00:06:28,710
As if I cut their throats myself.

47
00:06:29,080 --> 00:06:30,890
Maybe she managed to hide herself.

48
00:06:30,920 --> 00:06:32,470
I thought all of you was dead.

49
00:06:32,470 --> 00:06:34,690
You went north with Mormont and no one came back.

50
00:06:34,760 --> 00:06:36,180
Not for ages.

51
00:06:36,840 --> 00:06:38,150
But then you did.

52
00:06:40,150 --> 00:06:41,980
She survived Craster

53
00:06:41,980 --> 00:06:44,130
and he was the worst shit I've ever met.

54
00:06:44,400 --> 00:06:46,590
She survived the long march to the Wall.

55
00:06:46,590 --> 00:06:49,720
She survived a white walker, for fuck's sake.

56
00:06:51,260 --> 00:06:52,780
She might have got out.

57
00:06:55,560 --> 00:06:56,970
She might have.

58
00:06:58,950 --> 00:07:00,640
If they hit Mole's Town,

59
00:07:01,720 --> 00:07:03,320
then we're next.

60
00:07:06,390 --> 00:07:08,480
Mance and his army must be close.

61
00:07:08,480 --> 00:07:10,020
100,000 of them.

62
00:07:10,060 --> 00:07:12,770
And there's what, 105 of us left?

63
00:07:13,070 --> 00:07:15,460
You counting Black Jack, Kegs, and Mully?

64
00:07:16,580 --> 00:07:18,060
102.

65
00:07:18,880 --> 00:07:21,840
How do 102 men stop 100,000?

66
00:07:25,620 --> 00:07:28,330
Whoever dies last, be a good lad

67
00:07:28,340 --> 00:07:30,060
and burn the rest of us.

68
00:07:30,840 --> 00:07:32,550
Once I'm done with this world,

69
00:07:33,840 --> 00:07:35,710
I don't want to come back.

70
00:08:36,840 --> 00:08:38,530
You think he was spying on you?

71
00:08:38,680 --> 00:08:40,370
No, not spying.

72
00:08:40,370 --> 00:08:43,980
The Dothraki think outsiders are ridiculous taking shame in the naked body.

73
00:08:43,980 --> 00:08:47,480
They make love under the stars for the whole khalasar to see.

74
00:08:48,940 --> 00:08:50,450
Yes, Your Grace.

75
00:08:51,190 --> 00:08:53,060
But you are not Dothraki.

76
00:08:54,250 --> 00:08:55,290
No.

77
00:08:56,870 --> 00:08:58,570
Well, I don't see why it matters.

78
00:08:58,570 --> 00:09:00,040
Grey Worm isn't interested.

79
00:09:00,040 --> 00:09:02,940
None of the Unsullied care what's under our clothes.

80
00:09:05,830 --> 00:09:07,740
He was interested.

81
00:09:08,650 --> 00:09:09,850
What?

82
00:09:12,400 --> 00:09:14,810
I believe he was interested.

83
00:09:17,110 --> 00:09:19,160
When the slavers castrate the boys,

84
00:09:19,310 --> 00:09:21,070
do they take all of it?

85
00:09:21,500 --> 00:09:22,910
All of it?

86
00:09:23,280 --> 00:09:24,480
The,

87
00:09:25,060 --> 00:09:27,590
the pillar and the stones.

88
00:09:30,460 --> 00:09:32,090
I don't know, Your Grace.

89
00:09:33,350 --> 00:09:34,910
Haven't you ever wondered?

90
00:09:38,550 --> 00:09:40,980
Yes, Your Grace.

91
00:09:58,480 --> 00:09:59,770
Missandei.

92
00:10:16,240 --> 00:10:18,670
The lessons you give I in common tongue,

93
00:10:21,170 --> 00:10:23,750
these are precious to I.

94
00:10:23,860 --> 00:10:25,840
-To me.  -To me.

95
00:10:26,150 --> 00:10:28,570
I don't remember teaching you the word precious.

96
00:10:28,570 --> 00:10:31,640
Jorah the Andal, he teaches I,

97
00:10:32,030 --> 00:10:35,150
he teaches me this word.

98
00:10:36,390 --> 00:10:39,040
Do you remember the name you were given at birth?

99
00:10:39,280 --> 00:10:41,030
I remember nothing.

100
00:10:41,940 --> 00:10:43,460
Only Unsullied.

101
00:10:43,460 --> 00:10:45,060
When they cut you,

102
00:10:46,410 --> 00:10:48,130
do you remember that?

103
00:10:50,260 --> 00:10:51,720
I'm sorry.

104
00:10:52,860 --> 00:10:54,710
I'm sorry they did that to you.

105
00:10:54,710 --> 00:10:57,490
Why? Why sorry?

106
00:10:57,500 --> 00:11:00,140
It's a terrible thing to do to a boy.

107
00:11:05,390 --> 00:11:07,740
If the masters never cut me,

108
00:11:07,880 --> 00:11:09,890
I never am Unsullied.

109
00:11:09,980 --> 00:11:13,050
I never stand in the Plaza of Pride

110
00:11:13,050 --> 00:11:17,320
when Daenerys Stormborn orders us to kill the masters.

111
00:11:17,450 --> 00:11:20,510
I never am chosen to lead the Unsullied.

112
00:11:21,310 --> 00:11:25,690
I never meet Missandei from the island of Naath.

113
00:11:42,340 --> 00:11:44,390
I am sorry,

114
00:11:46,000 --> 00:11:47,340
for today.

115
00:11:48,650 --> 00:11:49,990
I am sorry.

116
00:12:36,060 --> 00:12:38,720
Kraken.

117
00:12:38,720 --> 00:12:41,380
Strong as long as they're in the sea.

118
00:12:41,860 --> 00:12:44,080
When you take them out of the water,

119
00:12:44,390 --> 00:12:45,710
no bones.

120
00:12:45,710 --> 00:12:47,590
They collapse under their proud weight

121
00:12:47,590 --> 00:12:49,930
and slump into a heap of nothing.

122
00:12:50,380 --> 00:12:52,110
You'd think they know that.

123
00:12:52,440 --> 00:12:55,110
Unfortunately, they're not very bright.

124
00:12:56,310 --> 00:12:57,560
What do you tell them?

125
00:12:58,790 --> 00:13:00,250
I'm Theon Greyjoy,

126
00:13:00,410 --> 00:13:03,620
son of Balon, heir to the Iron Islands.

127
00:13:03,620 --> 00:13:05,940
-And what are you really?  -I'm Reek.

128
00:13:07,330 --> 00:13:08,220
Are you sure?

129
00:13:09,640 --> 00:13:12,030
You do look very much like a lord.

130
00:13:12,600 --> 00:13:15,410
Formidable, proud.

131
00:13:17,550 --> 00:13:18,300
I'm Reek.

132
00:13:18,560 --> 00:13:19,530
Until when?

133
00:13:20,780 --> 00:13:21,590
Always.

134
00:13:22,650 --> 00:13:24,280
-Forever.  -That's right.

135
00:13:25,730 --> 00:13:27,800
Until you're rotting in the ground.

136
00:13:31,330 --> 00:13:34,630
Remember what you are and what you're not.

137
00:13:35,580 --> 00:13:36,970
Bring me Moat Cailin.

138
00:14:07,190 --> 00:14:08,630
No closer.

139
00:14:12,120 --> 00:14:13,180
Who are you?

140
00:14:52,430 --> 00:14:53,260
I'm Kenning,

141
00:14:54,850 --> 00:14:56,250
commander of this garrison.

142
00:14:58,760 --> 00:15:01,470
-And you say you're Theon Greyjoy?  -Yes.

143
00:15:03,640 --> 00:15:05,050
And why should I believe that?

144
00:15:06,250 --> 00:15:08,790
I was born on Pyke to Balon Greyjoy.

145
00:15:09,080 --> 00:15:11,350
His third and last living son.

146
00:15:11,400 --> 00:15:12,530
I am your prince.

147
00:15:13,200 --> 00:15:15,030
I swear it by the Drowned God.

148
00:15:15,620 --> 00:15:17,350
What is dead may never die.

149
00:15:17,350 --> 00:15:18,870
What is dead may never die.

150
00:15:19,770 --> 00:15:21,230
And if you were my prince,

151
00:15:22,100 --> 00:15:24,300
why are you marching with a Bolton army?

152
00:15:24,300 --> 00:15:26,530
Lord Bolton took me captive after Winterfell.

153
00:15:27,460 --> 00:15:31,350
He sent me to treat with you in good faith as your fellow ironborn.

154
00:15:31,460 --> 00:15:33,340
And what does Lord Bolton want?

155
00:15:36,530 --> 00:15:38,130
You are fading from sickness,

156
00:15:38,220 --> 00:15:39,920
you are badly outnumbered,

157
00:15:39,920 --> 00:15:42,020
and you're hundreds of miles from the sea.

158
00:15:42,020 --> 00:15:44,230
Lord Bolton implores you to protect your men

159
00:15:44,230 --> 00:15:46,860
and abandon this fortress you can no longer hold.

160
00:15:48,090 --> 00:15:50,920
Do this, and he will be just and fair with you

161
00:15:50,920 --> 00:15:52,010
as he has been with me.

162
00:15:55,010 --> 00:15:58,050
The Boltons will give you safe passage to the Stony Shore.

163
00:15:58,290 --> 00:16:00,180
He wants us to surrender?

164
00:16:00,820 --> 00:16:02,700
My own father, your king,

165
00:16:03,800 --> 00:16:05,930
surrendered years ago to Robert Baratheon.

166
00:16:06,730 --> 00:16:08,280
I watched him bend the knee.

167
00:16:09,340 --> 00:16:10,700
There was no shame there.

168
00:16:10,820 --> 00:16:13,050
He fought with honor, as did you.

169
00:16:17,180 --> 00:16:19,330
"No shame." "Fought with honor."

170
00:16:19,740 --> 00:16:21,390
I'm sorry, I didn't hear.

171
00:16:23,810 --> 00:16:26,130
"No shame." "Fought with honor."

172
00:16:30,120 --> 00:16:32,450
Only a whipped dog would speak this way.

173
00:16:35,010 --> 00:16:35,770
Or a woman.

174
00:16:37,930 --> 00:16:39,330
Are you a woman, boy?

175
00:16:40,320 --> 00:16:40,970
You don't know.

176
00:16:40,970 --> 00:16:43,030
The ironborn will not surrender.

177
00:16:43,960 --> 00:16:45,240
Reek. My name is Reek.

178
00:16:45,240 --> 00:16:47,300
You go tell your master that,

179
00:16:47,570 --> 00:16:51,990
Theon Greyjoy, or whoever the fuck you are.

180
00:16:52,220 --> 00:16:53,140
My name is Reek.

181
00:16:53,620 --> 00:16:55,230
What in the hell are you muttering?

182
00:16:55,230 --> 00:16:56,220
I'm Reek.

183
00:16:58,600 --> 00:16:59,240
Reek.

184
00:17:06,900 --> 00:17:08,390
If we yield, we live?

185
00:17:09,000 --> 00:17:10,700
Is that what it says on this paper here?

186
00:17:10,880 --> 00:17:14,560
Yes. Have your men raise the white flag and open the gates.

187
00:17:16,020 --> 00:17:16,890
You're going home.

188
00:17:24,520 --> 00:17:26,440
You didn't really think I'd let them go, did you?

189
00:17:27,630 --> 00:17:30,310
It's fallen out of fashion, flaying.

190
00:17:30,530 --> 00:17:32,120
Sad, but true.

191
00:17:32,910 --> 00:17:34,270
Traditions are important.

192
00:17:35,430 --> 00:17:37,050
Where are we without our history?

193
00:17:37,310 --> 00:17:39,310
-Eh?  -Yes, my lord.

194
00:17:40,790 --> 00:17:41,780
Will we go home now?

195
00:17:43,520 --> 00:17:44,640
I believe we will.

196
00:17:45,500 --> 00:17:46,830
To our new home.

197
00:17:57,860 --> 00:18:00,230
You have foreign blood, don't you, Baelish?

198
00:18:00,560 --> 00:18:02,980
A great-grandfather from Braavos, yes.

199
00:18:04,770 --> 00:18:08,720
I suppose all of our ancestors came from somewhere else originally.

200
00:18:08,840 --> 00:18:12,220
Our forebearers settled the Vale thousands of years ago.

201
00:18:12,470 --> 00:18:14,640
We've fought off invaders ever since.

202
00:18:14,650 --> 00:18:16,090
The beauty of the Vale is matched only

203
00:18:16,090 --> 00:18:18,400
by the nobility of its great families.

204
00:18:19,240 --> 00:18:21,160
Lady Arryn often told me

205
00:18:21,210 --> 00:18:23,260
that you were her rock, lord Royce.

206
00:18:23,320 --> 00:18:25,910
She told me nothing about you, Baelish.

207
00:18:26,770 --> 00:18:28,610
But I didn't need to hear from her.

208
00:18:29,250 --> 00:18:31,210
Moneylender. Whoremonger.

209
00:18:31,210 --> 00:18:34,210
You've been licking Tywin Lannister's boots so long,

210
00:18:34,210 --> 00:18:35,860
-it's a wonder your tongue's not black.  -My lord.

211
00:18:35,860 --> 00:18:38,690
And when Jon Arryn named you Master of Coin,

212
00:18:38,740 --> 00:18:39,870
no one cared.

213
00:18:40,550 --> 00:18:44,280
Always been a grubby job. Why not let a grubby man do it?

214
00:18:44,400 --> 00:18:46,780
But when I heard you were lurking here,

215
00:18:46,920 --> 00:18:48,830
fawning over the Lady Arryn.

216
00:18:48,840 --> 00:18:50,710
Lady Arryn invited me.

217
00:18:51,270 --> 00:18:53,470
She and I have been close since childhood.

218
00:18:53,470 --> 00:18:55,560
Yes, we all know how close you were.

219
00:18:56,330 --> 00:18:58,900
Lady Arryn's predilections were her own affair.

220
00:18:58,910 --> 00:19:00,760
Her death is our affair.

221
00:19:00,760 --> 00:19:03,860
Of course. Her suicide shattered us all.

222
00:19:04,240 --> 00:19:07,870
She was an odd fish. Everyone knew that.

223
00:19:07,940 --> 00:19:11,810
But suicide? She adored that boy of hers.

224
00:19:12,030 --> 00:19:14,940
I don't see her abandoning him. Not by choice.

225
00:19:14,940 --> 00:19:17,710
Strange that within days of your arrival,

226
00:19:17,720 --> 00:19:22,140
you've married Lady Arryn and she's fallen through the Moon Door.

227
00:19:22,140 --> 00:19:24,280
She was always prone to melancholy.

228
00:19:25,030 --> 00:19:27,970
My lady wasn't meant for a world as brutal as ours.

229
00:19:28,110 --> 00:19:30,250
We were told there was a witness. A girl.

230
00:19:30,320 --> 00:19:32,420
A niece of yours, I believe.

231
00:19:34,410 --> 00:19:36,790
A girl with no learning and scattered wits.

232
00:19:36,790 --> 00:19:38,340
I assure you, she would be of no help.

233
00:19:38,340 --> 00:19:39,570
We'd like to speak with her.

234
00:19:42,730 --> 00:19:44,350
-Let me fetch her.  -No need.

235
00:19:45,220 --> 00:19:48,920
We prefer to hear her testimony unadulterated.

236
00:19:59,070 --> 00:20:00,230
Come closer, child.

237
00:20:00,750 --> 00:20:03,970
You have nothing to fear from us or him.

238
00:20:04,600 --> 00:20:07,180
Lord Baelish here is your uncle?

239
00:20:08,300 --> 00:20:09,980
Your name is Alayne?

240
00:20:11,780 --> 00:20:13,410
Perhaps you would feel more comfortable

241
00:20:13,410 --> 00:20:15,110
if Lord Baelish left the room.

242
00:20:15,140 --> 00:20:16,640
-My lady.  -I wasn't asking you.

243
00:20:16,640 --> 00:20:19,800
-He can stay.  -Speak up, girl, you're not a damn kitchen mouse.

244
00:20:19,910 --> 00:20:21,090
Tell us what you saw.

245
00:20:25,430 --> 00:20:26,690
I'm sorry, Lord Baelish.

246
00:20:27,650 --> 00:20:29,250
I have to tell the truth.

247
00:20:34,530 --> 00:20:35,760
I'll tell you everything.

248
00:20:36,470 --> 00:20:39,850
Please, Alayne, leave nothing out.

249
00:20:42,620 --> 00:20:44,250
My name is not Alayne.

250
00:20:45,510 --> 00:20:47,000
It's Sansa Stark,

251
00:20:47,230 --> 00:20:49,490
eldest daughter of Lord Eddard Stark.

252
00:20:50,530 --> 00:20:52,790
Lord Royce, we met when you came to Winterfell.

253
00:20:53,010 --> 00:20:55,560
You were escorting your son Ser Waymar to the Wall.

254
00:20:56,280 --> 00:20:57,690
Sansa Stark?

255
00:20:59,340 --> 00:21:02,270
You tell lies right to my face, you little worm?

256
00:21:02,270 --> 00:21:04,500
Lord Baelish has told many lies.

257
00:21:08,120 --> 00:21:09,560
All to protect me.

258
00:21:11,630 --> 00:21:13,640
Since my father was executed,

259
00:21:13,640 --> 00:21:16,330
I have been a hostage in King's Landing.

260
00:21:17,100 --> 00:21:21,160
A plaything for Joffrey to torture or Queen Cersei to torment.

261
00:21:21,520 --> 00:21:24,130
They beat me, they humiliated me,

262
00:21:24,130 --> 00:21:26,010
they married me to the Imp.

263
00:21:27,640 --> 00:21:29,690
I had no friends in King's Landing,

264
00:21:32,110 --> 00:21:33,120
except one.

265
00:21:39,890 --> 00:21:41,070
He saved me.

266
00:21:42,410 --> 00:21:45,100
Smuggled me away when he had the chance.

267
00:21:46,980 --> 00:21:49,250
He knew I'd be safe here in the Eyrie

268
00:21:49,720 --> 00:21:51,650
with my own blood, my Aunt Lysa.

269
00:21:53,850 --> 00:21:56,620
The Lannisters have friends everywhere.

270
00:21:56,620 --> 00:21:57,850
Even the Vale.

271
00:21:58,030 --> 00:22:01,010
He made me swear not to tell anyone my true name.

272
00:22:01,590 --> 00:22:03,770
Your secret is safe with us, my lady.

273
00:22:03,770 --> 00:22:06,520
Your father grew up right here in these halls.

274
00:22:06,560 --> 00:22:08,360
We hunted together many times.

275
00:22:08,710 --> 00:22:10,140
He was a fine man.

276
00:22:11,400 --> 00:22:14,700
Tell us what happened to your aunt, Sansa.

277
00:22:17,180 --> 00:22:19,900
You knew her well, my lords, my lady.

278
00:22:20,810 --> 00:22:22,640
You knew she was a troubled woman.

279
00:22:22,830 --> 00:22:25,000
She always loved Lord Baelish.

280
00:22:25,000 --> 00:22:26,490
She told me herself.

281
00:22:26,710 --> 00:22:29,270
From the moment he arrived at the gates of Riverrun,

282
00:22:29,270 --> 00:22:33,000
a boy of eight carrying everything he owned in a little sack.

283
00:22:34,390 --> 00:22:37,740
She confessed to me she never loved Lord Arryn.

284
00:22:38,770 --> 00:22:41,850
She did as her father commanded, as so many of us have.

285
00:22:42,860 --> 00:22:45,800
When the gods finally allowed her to be with Lord Baelish,

286
00:22:45,800 --> 00:22:47,080
she was so happy.

287
00:22:48,220 --> 00:22:49,000
For a time.

288
00:22:50,540 --> 00:22:53,230
My aunt was a jealous lady.

289
00:22:54,990 --> 00:22:59,540
She was terrified that Lord Baelish didn't love her anymore.

290
00:22:59,540 --> 00:23:01,850
That he would abandon her for a younger woman.

291
00:23:06,000 --> 00:23:06,850
And then,

292
00:23:08,150 --> 00:23:11,420
one day she saw him kiss me.

293
00:23:11,560 --> 00:23:12,470
Lady Sansa.

294
00:23:12,470 --> 00:23:15,080
It was a peck on the cheek, Lord Royce, nothing more.

295
00:23:16,580 --> 00:23:19,670
Lord Baelish is my uncle now, in truth, by marriage.

296
00:23:20,410 --> 00:23:22,240
He's always been so kind to me.

297
00:23:22,780 --> 00:23:25,110
I was so happy to be here, to be free.

298
00:23:25,900 --> 00:23:26,980
All because of him.

299
00:23:28,070 --> 00:23:29,960
But my aunt turned on me.

300
00:23:29,960 --> 00:23:33,110
She cursed me. Called me a whore.

301
00:23:33,110 --> 00:23:35,400
Promised to throw me through the Moon Door.

302
00:23:36,550 --> 00:23:38,420
When Lord Baelish tried to calm her,

303
00:23:38,430 --> 00:23:39,900
she struck him.

304
00:23:40,610 --> 00:23:41,940
She said she didn't want to live anymore.

305
00:23:41,940 --> 00:23:43,750
She stood on the edge of that Moon Door.

306
00:23:43,910 --> 00:23:45,710
He tried to reason with her.

307
00:23:45,910 --> 00:23:48,160
Promised her she was the only one he had ever loved,

308
00:23:48,160 --> 00:23:52,930
but she stepped through those doors and she was.

309
00:23:57,540 --> 00:24:00,840
Shh, it's not your fault, sweet girl.

310
00:24:05,930 --> 00:24:09,030
It's not your fault.

311
00:24:24,500 --> 00:24:26,730
You could see it in the way she raised that boy.

312
00:24:26,730 --> 00:24:29,530
Feeding him from her own teats when he was 10 years old.

313
00:24:29,660 --> 00:24:32,630
Lord Royce! This is hardly the time.

314
00:24:32,850 --> 00:24:34,280
Apologies, my lady.

315
00:24:34,860 --> 00:24:36,420
And to you as well, Baelish.

316
00:24:36,420 --> 00:24:38,280
We treated you a bit harshly.

317
00:24:38,280 --> 00:24:40,080
You want justice, Lord Royce.

318
00:24:40,080 --> 00:24:41,560
I can hardly complain about that.

319
00:24:42,170 --> 00:24:43,190
I want the same.

320
00:24:43,510 --> 00:24:48,190
Not much justice to be meted out in suicide, is there?

321
00:24:48,190 --> 00:24:50,000
For Lysa, no. But for her son?

322
00:24:50,250 --> 00:24:52,650
Only 20 years ago, the knights of the Vale

323
00:24:52,650 --> 00:24:55,970
rode behind Jon Arryn, Ned Stark, Robert Baratheon.

324
00:24:56,240 --> 00:24:59,040
They fought together to overcome the Mad King.

325
00:24:59,460 --> 00:25:01,630
And since then, Arryn and Royce,

326
00:25:01,750 --> 00:25:03,080
Corbray, Waynwood,

327
00:25:03,080 --> 00:25:06,290
all the great houses of the Vale watched from the corner.

328
00:25:06,290 --> 00:25:08,320
A timid boy at a tavern brawl.

329
00:25:08,810 --> 00:25:10,860
Are you questioning our courage?

330
00:25:11,630 --> 00:25:13,320
I want to know which side you're on.

331
00:25:14,150 --> 00:25:15,070
Do you support the Lannisters,

332
00:25:15,070 --> 00:25:17,420
the house that executed your friend Ned Stark?

333
00:25:17,420 --> 00:25:19,720
Of course we don't support the damn Lannisters.

334
00:25:19,720 --> 00:25:23,380
No? Catelyn Stark begged her sister for support and Lysa refused.

335
00:25:23,830 --> 00:25:26,480
By staying out of the fray, you've allowed Tywin Lannister

336
00:25:26,480 --> 00:25:29,300
to destroy his rivals on every compass point.

337
00:25:29,380 --> 00:25:30,790
Who stands against him now?

338
00:25:31,000 --> 00:25:33,340
Who would you have us back, Lord Baelish?

339
00:25:33,470 --> 00:25:35,290
Robb Stark is dead.

340
00:25:35,330 --> 00:25:37,340
I'd have you back Robin Arryn,

341
00:25:38,190 --> 00:25:39,290
Lord of the Vale.

342
00:25:39,370 --> 00:25:41,520
Robin Arryn is a sickly little boy.

343
00:25:41,650 --> 00:25:44,700
And sickly little boys sometimes become powerful men.

344
00:25:44,980 --> 00:25:46,630
More often they die young.

345
00:25:47,150 --> 00:25:49,660
I adored Lysa with all my heart.

346
00:25:49,980 --> 00:25:53,560
But she loved her son so much, she became overprotective.

347
00:25:54,010 --> 00:25:56,270
He needs to learn how to swing a sword.

348
00:25:56,270 --> 00:25:57,670
How to ride a horse.

349
00:25:57,710 --> 00:26:00,680
-Aye, it's time.  -Yes, it's time.

350
00:26:01,200 --> 00:26:02,640
Time for him to tour the Vale,

351
00:26:02,640 --> 00:26:04,970
to visit all the castles in his domain.

352
00:26:05,450 --> 00:26:08,400
Time for Robin to leave the nest.

353
00:26:28,200 --> 00:26:29,520
Ser Barristan.

354
00:26:30,320 --> 00:26:31,170
Yes?

355
00:26:33,800 --> 00:26:34,880
Who sent you?

356
00:27:11,090 --> 00:27:13,060
-Ser Barristan.  -Ser Jorah.

357
00:27:14,260 --> 00:27:16,220
Have I forgotten a council meeting?

358
00:27:16,350 --> 00:27:17,180
No.

359
00:27:27,270 --> 00:27:28,320
What's this?

360
00:27:28,610 --> 00:27:29,960
A royal pardon

361
00:27:30,950 --> 00:27:32,770
signed by Robert Baratheon.

362
00:27:47,070 --> 00:27:48,370
You spied on her.

363
00:27:51,430 --> 00:27:52,740
Who gave you this?

364
00:27:53,120 --> 00:27:54,330
Does it matter?

365
00:28:03,990 --> 00:28:04,830
Have you told her?

366
00:28:04,830 --> 00:28:07,560
I wanted to tell you first, man-to-man,

367
00:28:08,720 --> 00:28:10,290
rather than go behind your back.

368
00:28:14,210 --> 00:28:15,800
Let me speak with her in private.

369
00:28:15,800 --> 00:28:17,740
You'll never be alone with her again.

370
00:28:54,790 --> 00:28:56,750
Why did the usurper pardon you?

371
00:29:00,320 --> 00:29:01,610
If we could speak alone.

372
00:29:01,610 --> 00:29:04,270
No, speak to me here.

373
00:29:05,150 --> 00:29:06,870
Explain it to me.

374
00:29:06,950 --> 00:29:09,050
Who do you think sent this to Meereen?

375
00:29:09,370 --> 00:29:10,700
Who profits?

376
00:29:10,920 --> 00:29:13,320
This is the work of Tywin Lannister.

377
00:29:13,330 --> 00:29:15,050
He wants to divide us.

378
00:29:15,280 --> 00:29:17,760
If we're fighting each other, we're not fighting him.

379
00:29:17,760 --> 00:29:20,520
The pardon was signed the year we met.

380
00:29:22,510 --> 00:29:23,810
Why were you pardoned?

381
00:29:23,810 --> 00:29:26,190
Unless you're saying this document was forged.

382
00:29:29,420 --> 00:29:30,840
It is not forged.

383
00:29:30,920 --> 00:29:31,970
Why, then?

384
00:29:32,550 --> 00:29:34,620
I sent letters to Varys,

385
00:29:34,790 --> 00:29:37,000
the spymaster of King's Landing.

386
00:29:37,450 --> 00:29:39,510
What was the content of these letters?

387
00:29:39,760 --> 00:29:41,670
-Information.  -What information?

388
00:29:42,410 --> 00:29:44,830
When you and Viserys arrived in Pentos.

389
00:29:45,330 --> 00:29:47,570
His plan to marry you to Khal Drogo.

390
00:29:47,570 --> 00:29:48,860
When you were married.

391
00:29:49,600 --> 00:29:51,200
When your brother died.

392
00:29:51,670 --> 00:29:53,980
You told him I was carrying Drogo's child?

393
00:29:54,430 --> 00:29:55,410
-I.  -Yes or no?

394
00:29:55,410 --> 00:29:56,650
-Khaleesi.  -Don't call me that.

395
00:29:56,660 --> 00:29:59,770
Did you tell him I was carrying Drogo's child?

396
00:30:03,210 --> 00:30:04,060
Yes.

397
00:30:06,620 --> 00:30:09,270
That wine merchant tried to poison me,

398
00:30:09,270 --> 00:30:10,500
because of your information.

399
00:30:10,500 --> 00:30:12,260
I stopped you from drinking his wine.

400
00:30:12,260 --> 00:30:14,440
Because you knew it was poisoned.

401
00:30:15,550 --> 00:30:16,350
I suspected.

402
00:30:16,350 --> 00:30:17,980
You betrayed me

403
00:30:19,490 --> 00:30:20,990
from the first.

404
00:30:21,550 --> 00:30:22,880
Forgive me.

405
00:30:24,430 --> 00:30:25,510
I never meant.

406
00:30:27,030 --> 00:30:28,360
please, Khaleesi, forgive me.

407
00:30:28,360 --> 00:30:31,850
You sold my secrets to the man who killed my father

408
00:30:31,860 --> 00:30:33,620
-and stole my brother's throne.  -I have protected you.

409
00:30:33,620 --> 00:30:36,370
-Fought for you. Killed for you.  -And you want me to forgive you?

410
00:30:39,310 --> 00:30:40,550
I have loved you.

411
00:30:40,690 --> 00:30:41,560
Love?

412
00:30:43,430 --> 00:30:46,080
Love? How can you say that to me?

413
00:30:46,160 --> 00:30:48,720
Any other man, and I would have you executed.

414
00:30:48,720 --> 00:30:50,590
But you, I do not want you in my city

415
00:30:50,590 --> 00:30:52,420
dead or alive.

416
00:30:52,430 --> 00:30:55,150
Go back to your masters in King's Landing.

417
00:30:55,150 --> 00:30:57,640
Collect your pardon if you can.

418
00:31:01,430 --> 00:31:02,240
Daenerys, please.

419
00:31:02,240 --> 00:31:05,980
Don't ever presume to touch me again

420
00:31:05,980 --> 00:31:07,330
or speak my name.

421
00:31:07,340 --> 00:31:09,160
You have until dusk to collect your things

422
00:31:09,170 --> 00:31:10,840
and leave this city.

423
00:31:10,840 --> 00:31:13,490
If you're found in Meereen past break of day,

424
00:31:13,500 --> 00:31:16,280
I'll have your head thrown into Slaver's Bay.

425
00:31:19,250 --> 00:31:20,080
Go.

426
00:31:22,600 --> 00:31:23,450
Now.

427
00:32:19,230 --> 00:32:21,680
Moat Cailin is yours, Father.

428
00:32:28,900 --> 00:32:30,100
Walk with me.

429
00:32:30,950 --> 00:32:32,890
Has there been any word from Locke?

430
00:32:33,490 --> 00:32:34,320
No.

431
00:32:34,900 --> 00:32:36,080
Unimportant.

432
00:32:36,190 --> 00:32:38,290
A cripple, a young boy.

433
00:32:39,240 --> 00:32:41,220
None of the northern lords have seen them.

434
00:32:42,530 --> 00:32:43,880
Dead most likely.

435
00:32:46,400 --> 00:32:48,310
Most of the ironborn have fled the North.

436
00:32:49,580 --> 00:32:52,930
Now more will follow, thanks to you.

437
00:32:55,720 --> 00:32:57,150
Tell me, what you see?

438
00:33:00,500 --> 00:33:05,110
Moors, fields, hills.

439
00:33:06,020 --> 00:33:07,710
Tell me, what you see?

440
00:33:12,290 --> 00:33:13,180
Nothing.

441
00:33:13,860 --> 00:33:14,880
Not nothing.

442
00:33:15,600 --> 00:33:16,690
The North.

443
00:33:17,800 --> 00:33:20,630
Ride 700 miles that way, you're still in the North.

444
00:33:21,620 --> 00:33:23,430
400 miles that way.

445
00:33:24,370 --> 00:33:26,090
300 miles that way.

446
00:33:26,090 --> 00:33:29,510
The North is larger than the other six kingdoms combined.

447
00:33:29,520 --> 00:33:31,500
And I am the Warden of the North.

448
00:33:32,170 --> 00:33:33,640
The North is mine.

449
00:33:36,360 --> 00:33:38,020
Now tell me, what is your name?

450
00:33:42,430 --> 00:33:44,010
Ramsay Snow.

451
00:33:44,640 --> 00:33:46,220
No, not Ramsay Snow.

452
00:33:47,950 --> 00:33:48,910
Open it.

453
00:33:50,280 --> 00:33:52,270
From this day until your last day,

454
00:33:52,480 --> 00:33:54,070
you are Ramsay Bolton,

455
00:33:54,710 --> 00:33:57,220
son of Roose Bolton, Warden of the North.

456
00:34:04,090 --> 00:34:05,300
You honor me.

457
00:34:06,450 --> 00:34:08,780
I swear I will uphold your name

458
00:34:08,810 --> 00:34:10,050
and your tradition.

459
00:34:11,390 --> 00:34:13,280
I will be worthy of you, Father,

460
00:34:14,370 --> 00:34:15,430
I promise.

461
00:34:34,430 --> 00:34:37,750
Come, Reek, I'll be needing a bath.

462
00:35:06,430 --> 00:35:07,360
Yes?

463
00:35:21,750 --> 00:35:24,160
First time I saw you, you were just a child.

464
00:35:24,160 --> 00:35:27,140
A girl from the North come to the capital for the first time.

465
00:35:27,860 --> 00:35:29,550
Not a child any longer.

466
00:35:33,900 --> 00:35:35,350
Why did you help me?

467
00:35:36,280 --> 00:35:37,870
They would have thrown you through the Moon Door

468
00:35:37,880 --> 00:35:39,410
if they found you guilty.

469
00:35:40,700 --> 00:35:42,100
That's not an answer.

470
00:35:45,590 --> 00:35:47,000
If they'd have executed you,

471
00:35:47,000 --> 00:35:48,520
what would they have done with me?

472
00:35:49,750 --> 00:35:51,110
I don't know.

473
00:35:52,120 --> 00:35:53,500
Neither do I.

474
00:35:55,850 --> 00:35:57,680
Better to gamble on the man you know

475
00:35:57,680 --> 00:35:59,460
than the strangers you don't?

476
00:36:01,550 --> 00:36:03,010
And you think you know me?

477
00:36:05,250 --> 00:36:06,700
I know what you want.

478
00:36:07,000 --> 00:36:07,930
Do you?

479
00:36:24,270 --> 00:36:25,770
I thought it'd make me happy,

480
00:36:26,200 --> 00:36:28,020
but it doesn't. Not really.

481
00:36:28,310 --> 00:36:29,920
Nothing makes you happy.

482
00:36:30,050 --> 00:36:31,700
-Lots of things make me happy.  -Like what?

483
00:36:31,700 --> 00:36:33,440
Killing Polliver, killing Rorge.

484
00:36:33,440 --> 00:36:37,170
So you're sad because you didn't get to kill Joffrey yourself.

485
00:36:37,300 --> 00:36:38,250
Is that it?

486
00:36:38,250 --> 00:36:40,020
At least I could have been there to watch.

487
00:36:40,170 --> 00:36:42,860
I wanted to see the look in his eyes when he knew it was over.

488
00:36:42,860 --> 00:36:46,000
Aye, nothing in the world beats that look.

489
00:36:47,210 --> 00:36:48,760
You protected him for most of his life.

490
00:36:48,760 --> 00:36:50,100
You think you could have saved him?

491
00:36:51,190 --> 00:36:53,240
I wasn't the damn wine taster.

492
00:36:55,580 --> 00:36:59,640
Little shit deserved to die, but poison,

493
00:37:00,490 --> 00:37:02,200
poison's a woman's weapon.

494
00:37:02,630 --> 00:37:04,300
Men kill with steel.

495
00:37:04,300 --> 00:37:06,120
That's your stupid pride talking.

496
00:37:06,120 --> 00:37:07,920
It's why you'll never be a great killer.

497
00:37:08,560 --> 00:37:11,270
I'd have killed Joffrey with a chicken bone if I had to.

498
00:37:12,740 --> 00:37:15,550
I'd pay good money to see that.

499
00:37:18,990 --> 00:37:20,430
You should have let me burn it.

500
00:37:21,720 --> 00:37:23,020
It's a fleabite.

501
00:37:24,620 --> 00:37:27,450
That fleabite's got you walking a lot slower than you used to.

502
00:37:27,660 --> 00:37:30,930
Well, we won't have to walk too much further.

503
00:37:31,190 --> 00:37:32,730
You really think my aunt will pay for me?

504
00:37:32,730 --> 00:37:34,250
Aye, she'll pay.

505
00:37:34,260 --> 00:37:35,740
I've never even met her.

506
00:37:36,240 --> 00:37:39,090
Doesn't matter. You're her blood.

507
00:37:40,650 --> 00:37:43,850
Family, honor, all that horseshit.

508
00:37:43,850 --> 00:37:46,360
It's all you lords and ladies ever talk about.

509
00:37:47,190 --> 00:37:48,360
I'm not a lady.

510
00:37:49,790 --> 00:37:51,780
Who would pass the Bloody Gate?

511
00:37:52,370 --> 00:37:55,440
The bloody Hound, Sandor Clegane.

512
00:37:55,610 --> 00:37:56,720
And his

513
00:37:58,260 --> 00:38:01,040
traveling companion Arya Stark,

514
00:38:01,040 --> 00:38:03,670
niece of your lady Lysa Arryn.

515
00:38:04,580 --> 00:38:06,260
Then I offer my condolences.

516
00:38:07,520 --> 00:38:08,930
Lady Arryn died.

517
00:38:12,410 --> 00:38:13,590
Three days ago.

518
00:38:32,560 --> 00:38:34,280
I've never left home before, Uncle Petyr.

519
00:38:34,290 --> 00:38:36,610
-I'm afraid to leave.  -You shouldn't be.

520
00:38:36,930 --> 00:38:39,850
The Lord of the Vale belongs in the Eyrie, Mother said.

521
00:38:40,040 --> 00:38:42,260
She said it's not safe outside.

522
00:38:42,260 --> 00:38:44,180
It wasn't safe for her inside.

523
00:38:44,900 --> 00:38:47,840
People die at their dinner tables.

524
00:38:47,840 --> 00:38:49,450
They die in their beds.

525
00:38:49,460 --> 00:38:52,590
They die squatting over their chamber pots.

526
00:38:53,100 --> 00:38:55,580
Everybody dies sooner or later.

527
00:38:55,580 --> 00:38:57,520
Don't worry about your death.

528
00:38:58,520 --> 00:39:00,230
Worry about your life.

529
00:39:00,970 --> 00:39:02,710
Take charge of your life

530
00:39:02,740 --> 00:39:04,600
for as long as it lasts.

531
00:39:05,380 --> 00:39:08,060
That is what it means to be Lord of the Vale.

532
00:39:32,330 --> 00:39:33,640
Shall we go?

533
00:39:41,700 --> 00:39:44,110
Wine always helps.

534
00:39:45,680 --> 00:39:47,140
I thank you for it.

535
00:39:49,700 --> 00:39:51,400
Trial by combat.

536
00:39:52,650 --> 00:39:55,890
Deciding a man's guilt or innocence

537
00:39:56,120 --> 00:39:57,710
in the eyes of the gods

538
00:39:57,970 --> 00:40:01,010
by having two other men hack each other to pieces.

539
00:40:01,280 --> 00:40:03,300
Tells you something about the gods.

540
00:40:06,120 --> 00:40:07,390
How much longer?

541
00:40:08,920 --> 00:40:09,800
Soon.

542
00:40:13,330 --> 00:40:15,310
Do you think Oberyn has a chance?

543
00:40:18,730 --> 00:40:19,850
The Red Viper of Dorne.

544
00:40:19,850 --> 00:40:22,170
You don't get a name like that unless you're deadly, right?

545
00:40:22,170 --> 00:40:23,520
I've never seen him fight.

546
00:40:23,520 --> 00:40:26,410
Oh, he's going to die. I'm going to die.

547
00:40:26,410 --> 00:40:27,710
Oberyn believes in himself.

548
00:40:27,710 --> 00:40:29,690
That's putting it mildly.

549
00:40:31,210 --> 00:40:33,180
What's the punishment for regicide?

550
00:40:33,180 --> 00:40:35,630
Drawing and quartering? Hanging?

551
00:40:36,490 --> 00:40:38,510
-Breaking at the wheel?  -Beheading.

552
00:40:38,510 --> 00:40:40,060
Seems rather ordinary.

553
00:40:40,290 --> 00:40:42,550
And he was my nephew as well, so what is that?

554
00:40:42,560 --> 00:40:44,300
Fratricide is brothers.

555
00:40:44,600 --> 00:40:46,310
Filicide is sons.

556
00:40:47,910 --> 00:40:49,770
Nepoticide. That's the one.

557
00:40:52,730 --> 00:40:55,490
Matricide, patricide,

558
00:40:55,620 --> 00:40:58,310
infanticide, suicide.

559
00:40:59,620 --> 00:41:02,110
There's no kind of killing that doesn't have its own word.

560
00:41:02,710 --> 00:41:03,740
Cousins.

561
00:41:03,740 --> 00:41:05,950
Cousins, you're right.

562
00:41:05,950 --> 00:41:07,930
There is no word for cousin killing.

563
00:41:08,270 --> 00:41:09,310
Well done.

564
00:41:10,240 --> 00:41:12,600
Do you remember cousin Orson? Orson Lannister?

565
00:41:12,600 --> 00:41:15,240
Of course. Wet-nurse dropped him on his head.

566
00:41:15,240 --> 00:41:17,020
-Left him simple.  -Simple?

567
00:41:17,410 --> 00:41:19,260
Used to sit all day in the garden.

568
00:41:19,260 --> 00:41:21,230
Crushing beetles with a rock.

569
00:41:26,060 --> 00:41:27,040
Nothing made him happier.

570
00:41:27,040 --> 00:41:28,620
Nothing made you happier.

571
00:41:28,900 --> 00:41:30,670
You'd think being tormented from birth

572
00:41:30,670 --> 00:41:32,760
would have given you some affinity for the afflicted.

573
00:41:32,760 --> 00:41:35,990
On the contrary. Laughing at another person's misery

574
00:41:35,990 --> 00:41:38,360
was the only thing that made me feel like everyone else.

575
00:41:38,550 --> 00:41:40,050
The joke wore thin, though.

576
00:41:40,050 --> 00:41:42,230
For you. You drifted away.

577
00:41:42,410 --> 00:41:43,870
I had other interests.

578
00:41:43,870 --> 00:41:45,880
Yes, other interests.

579
00:41:48,090 --> 00:41:49,550
But I stayed with Orson.

580
00:41:49,550 --> 00:41:50,470
Why?

581
00:41:51,680 --> 00:41:52,910
I was curious.

582
00:41:53,810 --> 00:41:55,460
Why was he smashing all those beetles?

583
00:41:55,460 --> 00:41:57,090
What did he get out of it?

584
00:41:57,370 --> 00:41:59,340
First thing I did was ask him.

585
00:41:59,650 --> 00:42:03,080
"Orson, why are you smashing all those beetles?"

586
00:42:03,230 --> 00:42:06,100
He gave me an answer. "Smash the beetles.

587
00:42:06,100 --> 00:42:07,330
Smash 'em."

588
00:42:10,240 --> 00:42:11,860
I wasn't deterred.

589
00:42:11,970 --> 00:42:13,540
I was the smartest person I knew.

590
00:42:13,550 --> 00:42:15,910
Certainly I had the wherewithal to unravel the mysteries

591
00:42:15,910 --> 00:42:17,450
that lay at the heart of a moron.

592
00:42:18,430 --> 00:42:20,960
So I went to Maester Volarik's library.

593
00:42:20,960 --> 00:42:23,280
Volarik. Tried to touch me once.

594
00:42:23,280 --> 00:42:25,960
Turns out, far too much has been written about great men

595
00:42:25,960 --> 00:42:28,090
and not nearly enough about morons.

596
00:42:28,590 --> 00:42:30,070
Doesn't seem right.

597
00:42:30,760 --> 00:42:32,160
In any case, I found nothing

598
00:42:32,160 --> 00:42:34,690
that illuminated the nature of Orson's affliction

599
00:42:34,690 --> 00:42:37,880
or the reason behind his relentless beetle slaughter.

600
00:42:37,920 --> 00:42:40,140
So I went back to the source.

601
00:42:40,140 --> 00:42:42,110
I may not have been able to speak with Orson,

602
00:42:42,110 --> 00:42:44,900
but I could observe him, watch him,

603
00:42:44,910 --> 00:42:46,890
the way men watch animals

604
00:42:46,890 --> 00:42:49,770
to come to a deeper understanding of their behavior.

605
00:42:52,480 --> 00:42:53,990
And as I watched,

606
00:42:54,650 --> 00:42:56,630
I became more and more sure of it.

607
00:42:57,210 --> 00:42:59,070
There was something happening there.

608
00:42:59,810 --> 00:43:02,520
His face was like the page of a book

609
00:43:02,520 --> 00:43:04,620
written in a language I didn't understand.

610
00:43:04,620 --> 00:43:07,230
But he wasn't mindless. He had his reasons.

611
00:43:08,010 --> 00:43:10,880
And I became possessed with knowing what they were.

612
00:43:10,880 --> 00:43:14,250
I began to spend inordinate amounts of time watching him.

613
00:43:15,420 --> 00:43:17,160
I would eat my lunch in the garden,

614
00:43:17,540 --> 00:43:20,630
chewing my mutton to the music of "Kuuh".

615
00:43:21,510 --> 00:43:24,150
And when I wasn't watching him, I was thinking about him.

616
00:43:24,220 --> 00:43:26,490
Father droned on about the family legacy

617
00:43:26,490 --> 00:43:28,470
and I thought about Orson's beetles.

618
00:43:28,500 --> 00:43:31,220
I read the histories of Targaryen conquests.

619
00:43:31,220 --> 00:43:33,090
Did I hear dragon wings? No.

620
00:43:33,090 --> 00:43:36,250
I heard "Kuuh".

621
00:43:36,550 --> 00:43:39,940
And I still couldn't figure out why he was doing it.

622
00:43:39,940 --> 00:43:42,940
And I had to know, because it was horrible

623
00:43:43,420 --> 00:43:45,760
that all these beetles should be dying for no reason.

624
00:43:45,760 --> 00:43:47,420
Every day, around the world,

625
00:43:47,420 --> 00:43:51,230
men, women, and children are murdered by the score.

626
00:43:51,240 --> 00:43:53,590
Who gives a dusty fuck about a bunch of beetles?

627
00:43:53,590 --> 00:43:56,690
I know, I know. But still, it filled me with dread.

628
00:43:57,430 --> 00:44:00,040
Piles and piles of them, years and years of them.

629
00:44:00,040 --> 00:44:02,050
How many countless living crawling things

630
00:44:02,050 --> 00:44:04,810
smashed and dried out and returned to the dirt?

631
00:44:05,900 --> 00:44:07,600
In my dreams I found myself

632
00:44:07,600 --> 00:44:10,080
standing on a beach made of beetle husks

633
00:44:10,090 --> 00:44:12,100
stretching as far as the eye could see.

634
00:44:12,530 --> 00:44:14,180
I woke up crying,

635
00:44:14,180 --> 00:44:16,710
weeping for their shattered little bodies.

636
00:44:17,410 --> 00:44:19,060
I tried to stop Orson once.

637
00:44:19,060 --> 00:44:20,170
He was twice your size.

638
00:44:20,180 --> 00:44:22,470
He just pushed me aside with a "Kuuh"

639
00:44:22,470 --> 00:44:24,060
and kept on smashing.

640
00:44:24,760 --> 00:44:27,270
Every day, until that mule

641
00:44:27,270 --> 00:44:29,210
kicked him in the chest and killed him.

642
00:44:40,400 --> 00:44:41,790
So what do you think?

643
00:44:43,550 --> 00:44:44,860
Why did he do it?

644
00:44:45,930 --> 00:44:47,400
What was it all about?

645
00:44:51,360 --> 00:44:52,510
I don't know.

646
00:45:11,760 --> 00:45:12,990
Good luck today.

647
00:45:46,440 --> 00:45:48,380
Looks like very light armor.

648
00:45:48,380 --> 00:45:49,650
I like to move around.

649
00:45:49,650 --> 00:45:51,510
You could at least wear a helmet.

650
00:45:53,390 --> 00:45:55,080
You shouldn't drink before a fight.

651
00:45:55,080 --> 00:45:57,690
You learn this during your years in the fighting pits?

652
00:45:58,070 --> 00:45:59,650
I always drink before a fight.

653
00:45:59,650 --> 00:46:02,690
It could get you killed. It could get me killed.

654
00:46:03,400 --> 00:46:05,300
Today is not the day I die.

655
00:46:12,800 --> 00:46:14,710
You're going to fight that?

656
00:46:15,080 --> 00:46:16,900
I'm going to kill that.

657
00:46:21,160 --> 00:46:22,900
He is the biggest man I've ever seen.

658
00:46:22,900 --> 00:46:25,700
Size does not matter when you are flat on your back.

659
00:46:25,700 --> 00:46:27,240
Thank the gods.

660
00:46:29,580 --> 00:46:32,550
In the sight of gods and men,

661
00:46:32,910 --> 00:46:35,040
we gather to ascertain

662
00:46:35,270 --> 00:46:38,150
the guilt or innocence of this

663
00:46:39,250 --> 00:46:42,020
man Tyrion Lannister.

664
00:46:42,240 --> 00:46:44,840
May the Mother grant them mercy.

665
00:46:44,840 --> 00:46:48,700
May the Father give them such justice as they deserve.

666
00:46:48,700 --> 00:46:51,170
And may the Warrior guide the hand,

667
00:46:51,170 --> 00:46:52,810
of our champion.

668
00:47:02,540 --> 00:47:04,520
Don't leave me alone in this world.

669
00:47:04,600 --> 00:47:05,510
Never.

670
00:47:27,070 --> 00:47:28,430
Have they told you who I am?

671
00:47:28,430 --> 00:47:30,100
Some dead man.

672
00:47:35,000 --> 00:47:38,360
I am the brother of Elia Martell.

673
00:47:38,490 --> 00:47:40,590
Do you know why I have come all the way to this stinking

674
00:47:40,600 --> 00:47:42,690
shit-pile of a city?

675
00:47:43,510 --> 00:47:44,510
For you.

676
00:47:49,680 --> 00:47:52,720
I'm going to hear you confess before you die.

677
00:47:53,070 --> 00:47:54,410
You raped my sister.

678
00:47:54,740 --> 00:47:55,930
You murdered her.

679
00:47:56,240 --> 00:47:57,670
You killed her children.

680
00:47:58,520 --> 00:48:01,010
Say it now and we can make this quick.

681
00:48:08,960 --> 00:48:09,960
Say it.

682
00:48:10,280 --> 00:48:11,630
You raped her.

683
00:48:12,690 --> 00:48:14,310
You murdered her.

684
00:48:18,140 --> 00:48:19,640
You killed her children.

685
00:48:31,240 --> 00:48:32,390
You raped her!

686
00:48:32,460 --> 00:48:33,660
You murdered her!

687
00:48:33,670 --> 00:48:35,600
You killed her children!

688
00:49:15,060 --> 00:49:16,450
You raped her!

689
00:49:16,830 --> 00:49:18,380
You murdered her!

690
00:49:27,800 --> 00:49:30,370
You killed her children!

691
00:49:37,720 --> 00:49:40,040
Wait. Are you dying?

692
00:49:40,040 --> 00:49:41,870
No, no, no.

693
00:49:41,870 --> 00:49:44,550
You can't die yet. You haven't confessed.

694
00:49:47,550 --> 00:49:48,670
Say it.

695
00:49:49,600 --> 00:49:52,800
Say her name. Elia Martell.

696
00:49:53,020 --> 00:49:55,640
You raped her. You killed her children.

697
00:49:55,640 --> 00:49:58,020
Elia Martell.

698
00:49:58,020 --> 00:50:00,000
Who gave you the order?

699
00:50:00,500 --> 00:50:02,630
Who gave you the order?!

700
00:50:03,200 --> 00:50:04,500
Say her name!

701
00:50:04,500 --> 00:50:07,020
You raped her! You murdered her!

702
00:50:07,020 --> 00:50:09,030
You killed her children.

703
00:50:09,690 --> 00:50:11,790
Say it. Say her name.

704
00:50:13,300 --> 00:50:14,370
Say it!

705
00:50:22,410 --> 00:50:24,110
Elia Martell.

706
00:50:25,600 --> 00:50:27,500
I killed her children.

707
00:50:27,800 --> 00:50:29,150
Then I raped her.

708
00:50:30,500 --> 00:50:33,580
Then I smashed her head in like this!

709
00:50:47,190 --> 00:50:49,400
The gods have made their will known.

710
00:50:50,300 --> 00:50:51,720
Tyrion Lannister,

711
00:50:52,380 --> 00:50:54,760
in the name of King Tommen of the House Baratheon,

712
00:50:54,770 --> 00:50:56,390
First of His Name,

713
00:50:57,290 --> 00:50:59,580
you are hereby sentenced to death.

